    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Iran says it has destroyed an early-warning radar in Bahrain, describing the attack as retaliation for a United States strike on telecommunication infrastructure on Sirik.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On November 13, Bahrain's Ministry of Foreign Affairs condemned what it described as Iran's renewed aggression after recent air strikes on Riffa Air Base.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385842480:66"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Earlier, on 28 February 2026, during the 2026 Iran war, Iran carried out retaliatory missile and drone strikes on Bahrain, hitting multiple buildings in Manama, including Juffair.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385842480:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The map shows Bandar Sirik, the location where the reports place the events.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: Islamic Resistance in Iraq and Jaysh al-Ghadab, and Defensive/precautionary.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385842480:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1385842480:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "According to Wikipedia's sources, casualties on the second side were 2 DOD employes wounded and 1 oil tanker damaged.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385842480:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "The report comes from Türkiye.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:01:04Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined it: “Iran says it targeted US military radar in Bahrain in retaliatory strike.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:guardian:a4db15e2b4ef"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-13T00:01:11Z",
